      "title": "Benchmark names do not identify the scientific operator",
      "observation": "MR is an integer modular primality/counting probe; MRC evaluates margin-ranking-loss gradients, while MRIQ forms weighted complex Fourier quantities. Muon is a matrix optimizer using Float32 state and BF16-stored iterates plus vendor GEMM. These source-backed identities prevent applying an imaging or particle-physics interpretation merely because of a short name. Vendor kernels remain unassigned unless exact source membership is proved; BF16 storage alone does not establish executed tensor arithmetic.",
